# Algo / Redis Lua parity

- `algo` is the pure-Go reference. Redis reimplements the same math in Lua (`redisstore/scripts.go`).
- Change both when altering algorithm behavior. Do not “fix” only one side.
- After edits, run `.agents/commands/parity-redis.md` (`TestAlgoRedisParity`).
- Redis clock is Redis `TIME`; sliding-log cutoffs and reset ceil-to-ms must stay aligned with `algo`.
